# Credentials — never commit these.
#
# .npmrc matters most: a project-level .npmrc holds the npm auth token, and
# committing it to a public repository publishes a credential with push access
# to every package this account owns.
.npmrc
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Build and dependency output
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Package tarballs. `npm pack` writes these into the repository root and the
# release tooling packs on every run, so one is easy to commit by accident.
*.tgz

# Visp's own working files, for when this repository is itself a target project.
# Anchored to the repository root: these names also exist under templates/ as
# the sources Visp installs, and an unanchored pattern silently ignores edits
# to them.
/.visp/
/.local-plans/
/AGENTS.visp.md
/AGENTS.visp-hyper.md
/visp-hyper-instructions.md

# Agent and assistant scratch
.claude/
.llm-memory/

# Editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.~lock.*#
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs and local overrides
*.log
*.local

# Personal planning documents that pre-date the planning workspace
Visp-Hyper-Agent-Comprehensive-Implementation-Plan.docx
